A KV cache, or key-value cache, in the context of Language Model (LLM) inference, stores previously generated tokens along with their corresponding attention scores to speed up the generation process for subsequent tokens. This caching technique helps improve the efficiency and throughput of the model without compromising the quality of the generated text.

